# Byte-pinned hook-registry fixtures must check out identically on every platform:
# Windows `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise convert LF to CRLF and change the
# bytes their checksums are pinned to. `-text` stops git transforming them.
csq-core/tests/fixtures/hook_registry_1b/** -text
csq-core/tests/fixtures/hook-registry/** -text

# codex-cli 0.159.2's real `threads` schema. Its trigger bodies are hashed byte-for-byte
# against `CODEX_OWN_TRIGGERS` (SHA-256 of the exact `sqlite_master.sql` text, measured from
# real LF databases); a CRLF checkout changed those bytes and the known-upstream schema
# refused (Windows CI run 38993121327). Keep the Git-object LF bytes on every platform.
csq-core/tests/fixtures/codex-state5-threads-0.159.2.sql -text

# Native libtest output intentionally ends pending test rows with a space.
# Preserve this SHA-bound literal frame and allow only its native trailing blanks.
scripts/tests/fixtures/proof-native-framing-r1-18.txt -text whitespace=-blank-at-eol

# Rust source always checks out with LF, on every platform: tests scan source text
# at fixed `\n` boundaries.
*.rs text eol=lf
